From 8a261ae8ae280ccca9525b810f4cc24ed17e889c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Simeon Marijon <simeon.marijon@foss.st.com>
Date: Tue, 5 Dec 2023 15:17:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 437/841] feat(st): use NVMEM framework instead of direct reg
 access

Previously all acces was done directly using tamp_bkpr which
calculate the offset on a hardcoded based address.

Now, we use a cell description from the device to access the TAMP
Backup Registers

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/arm-trusted-firmware.git 7a28c43be94bf31a89b8127061b417e0029abda2 feat(st): use NVMEM framework instead of direct reg access]
Signed-off-by: Simeon Marijon <simeon.marijon@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: I2e5fb0ad1c1a426e9d970313f5d773755ea14a5f
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/st/tf-a/+/344047
